ced visibility Identify and track third-party pixels and cookies continuously to instantly reveal hidden threats invisible to traditional tools Actions within iFrames Track what happens within embedded frames Window location manipulation Detect attempts to redirect users without their knowledge Compromised cookies Identify cookies vulnerable to exploitation Flags When Your Policy and Practice Don't Line Up The Dashboard highlights deviations between your privacy policy and actual code behavior, enabling easy comparison against GDPR, CPRA, and CCPA standards. Get a comprehensive map of all active components sorted by specific sensitive actions: When Marketing Adds Tools Without Privacy Review Discover all data-collecting trackers and scripts, and precisely map where personal data travels, including cross-border transfers. Detect any unauthorized marketing or analytics tools operating outside privacy oversight. When Your Practices Don’t Match Your Policies Leverage NLP to extract key privacy commitments from your public policy. This enables instant detection of deviations in live data behavior, allowing for comparison against standards like GDPR, CPRA, and CCPA. When Open Source and Third-Party Code Updates Remotely, Beyond Your Control Automatically and continuously monitor all third-party web apps and open source tools in production. Detect any changes executed remotely, even those beyond your direct oversight, that could potentially compromise your web environments. Reduces Regulatory Risk & Saves Time Automated Detection Our system automatically detects policy violations from unauthorized trackers and misaligned data flows, flagging site updates, vendor changes, and emerging risks. Continuous monitoring picks up remotely executed changes, even when code is controlled by others. Streamlined Operations Automates detection, validation, and reporting to slash manual work by up to 75% in the first quarter. Reports export directly to your privacy and legal teams, elimin